WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.251
Idea. Money in a bank can double every year. After x years you have two to the power x. When the unknown is in the power, it is an exponential equation.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:22.796
The special number e is about two point seven one eight. L N is the natural log key, the log to base e. L N of e to the k is just k. It undoes the power.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:31.509
To solve e to the two x equals four, take L N of both sides. Two x equals L N four, so x is L N two.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:45.279
An equation can hide a quadratic. E to the four x is e to the two x, squared. Let u be e to the two x. An exponential is always positive, so u is never zero or negative.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:53.391
In the exam you may meet two curves and an exact answer. Exact means an answer with L N in it, not a decimal.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:01:06.165
Method. Step one: for two curves, set the equations equal, and multiply to clear any negative power. Step two: let u be the exponential, and solve the quadratic.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:18.951
Step three: reject any u that is zero or negative. Step four: take L N and simplify. The trap: L N of five plus four is not L N five plus L N four.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:35.138
Worked example. November twenty twenty. Curve one is y equals five e to the minus two x plus four. Curve two is y equals e to the two x. They meet at A. Find the exact coordinates of A. Four marks.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:40.114
Step one: at A the y values are equal. Set the equations equal.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:49.318
Step two: multiply every term by e to the two x. This gives five, plus four e to the two x, equals e to the four x.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:02:00.705
Step three: let u be e to the two x. Then u squared minus four u minus five equals zero. This factorises as u minus five, times u plus one.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:13.169
Step four: u is five or minus one. But e to a power is always positive, so reject minus one. Then two x is L N five, so x is a half L N five.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:25.053
Step five: y is e to the two x, which is five. So A is a half L N five, five. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:34.375
A tempting wrong route is taking L N of both sides straight away. L N of a sum cannot be split. Clear the negative power first.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:44.000
Common mistake. A common mistake is keeping u equals minus one. You cannot take the log of a negative number. Reject it.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:57.385
Your turn. Now you try, from June twenty twenty two. Two curves meet at the origin O and at a point A. Show the hidden quadratic, then show that x at A is a third of L N nine.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:05.445
Here is Figure two: curve C and curve D, crossing at O and at A. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:15.638
Answer. Part one. At A the y values are equal. Multiply every term by e to the three x, then collect the terms on one side.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:30.454
Part two. Let u be e to the three x. Then u is one or nine. u equals one gives x equals nought, which is the origin. So at A, e to the three x is nine, and x is a third of L N nine.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:39.859
The most common wrong answer forgets to multiply the one and the nine by e to the three x. Then the printed quadratic never appears.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:47.184
Remember: match bases or take L N, clear negative powers, let u, reject u not above zero.
